title The sweep that read one spelling
prompt Autonomous fleet lap -- Petrichor seat, the lap after nine pens took the process id.
rota lap N was 4107 at the open, so N mod 5 is row 2 -- a row my own previous lap had already read today before advancing by hand to 3. I advanced by hand again to row 4: EARTH, Mercury, the concrete, the sense of aroma. Read the threshold, the clock and the mark, TWO_ROOMS, and the marked value. The row gave the lap its method before it had a subject -- the concrete fact is read off the face, at the door, ahead of any argument -- and the whole lap turned out to be one long application of it.
think THE COLD OPEN ANSWERED TWO REDS AND ONE OF THEM WAS THE OTHER REPORTING IT. standing_equipment read runs_red=1 naming amphora_restore_negative, so there was one real red, and it was in a lane that is not mine. Reds first outranks lane, and claim-as-override lets me name the claim rather than route around it.
think GREEN ALONE AND RED IN COMPANY IS A SIGNATURE, SO I RAN IT ALONE FIRST. The witness passed in 80 seconds, minutes after the roster had it fail at rneg: tamper refusal must leave no out-home. Then I read its source: let home = "/tmp/amphora_rneg_home" on line 11, and rm -rf home on line 15.
think THIS IS THE CLASS MY OWN PREVIOUS LAP CLOSED, AND MY CLOSE COUNTED ONE SPELLING. That sweep read TMPDIR= assignments in shell fixtures and repaired nine files. A Rishi let-string is a different spelling and the grep never saw it. Nine was not a count of the class; it was a count of what one grep could see.
think A LANTERN THAT FIRES TWICE BECOMES A LOOM, AND THIS ONE HAS FIRED THREE TIMES IN TWO LAPS. signal_trap and tlb_reach reddened one cold open, amphora_restore_negative the next. So the lap is a repair plus a meter, rather than a repair plus a wider sweep -- 64 files across five lanes is not one lap's worth of edits, and a ceiling records them where a memory would not.
think THE PROOF IS THE DIFFERENCE, NOT EITHER SIDE. I ran the elder as two concurrent copies and one of two failed at line 48, the exact assertion the roster reported; I ran the repaired file as two concurrent copies and both passed. Elder alone was green. A fault of location repeats and a race does not, so the concurrent-versus-alone difference is the discriminator rather than either reading by itself.
obs THE CONTROL CAUGHT MY OWN SCAN COUNTING THE TREE TWICE, AND BOTH READINGS WOULD HAVE INSTRUCTED A REPAIR ALREADY MADE OR NEVER NEEDED. Two of twenty-one behaviors failed on the first run: pid_free and interpolate_free. The token class /tmp/[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+ stops at $, so /tmp/pen_$$ matched as the constant /tmp/pen_ and counted -- five of those files are ones I repaired last lap, so the guard was reporting damage where the repair had landed. One character of lookahead moved 69 -> 64. Then the hot pass reddened on my own control: text inside single quotes is TEXT, and a control writing a plant into a throwaway tree or a scan normalising a path bwrap made is talking about a path rather than claiming one. Exactly four files carry that shape, seventeen sites, every one a control or a scan, two of them this guard's own -- 64 -> 61 files and 308 sites. That is %519's shape one room over, found by the same means: the control.
obs THE WIPING SUBSET IS READ SEPARATELY BECAUSE THE TWO FAILURES DIFFER IN KIND. A file that only writes a constant pen may interleave with a peer and survive; a file that rm -rf's one takes the peer's in-flight state down. Seven files wipe today, eight before this repair, and that is the ceiling worth driving to zero first because it is small enough to.
obs THE EARTH ROW'S METHOD CLOSED A FRAME RATHER THAN OPENING ONE. context/CIVIC_STYLE.md read C+/78 and pushed a molt frame -- and at Field, the class its siblings hold, it reads B/83 and stands. Measurement at molt time is allowed to close a frame, so no rewrite was spent on a page already inside its budget. What the reading found instead is that the letter depended on a flag I typed.
obs qa_report_card.sh NEVER READS THE SETTING A PAGE DECLARES IN ITS OWN HEAD. setting=field is assigned at line 116 and a typed --setting overrides it; nothing reads the file. Measured over 1,520 living tracked Markdown pages, 305 declare a Gauge setting in their first twelve lines -- 44 Door, 260 Field, 1 Meter. Of the 44 Door-declared, 13 read a different letter at their own declaration than at the default, and every one of the 13 is loose in the same direction, because Door is the strictest class and field is the default. Three cross the B door: constel/README.md C+ against B, and the fascia-and-the-way-home and mitra-shed foundations, C and C+ against B. A grade below B is what pushes a molt frame, so the miss can only ever let a page through.
obs I DID NOT BUILD THAT FIX, AND THE REASON IS THE SHAPE OF THE DECLARATION RATHER THAN ITS SIZE. Honouring a declared Door is honouring a stricter reading and costs nothing; honouring a declared Meter would set register and reach to 100 on a page's own word, which is a self-granted exemption, and this card already refuses one of those by name. Which of the three a page may declare itself into is a rule rather than a repair, so it goes to Keaton with its number.
obs THE HOT PASS CAUGHT A PEER'S SHELF LINK, AND THE GUARD THAT CAUGHT IT NAMES THE REPAIR IN ITS REFUSAL. fold_shelf_link reddened on construction/archive/20260906-222720_itinerary-landed-accounts.md, which arrived on my rebase carrying a link that kept the depth of the card it was folded out of -- archive/REDS-...-510.md from a file already standing in archive/. Repaired in place; the guard's own header rules that lawful, since nothing moved and only the text did. Not mine to write, mine to find.
obs THE PIN AND THE CARD BOTH FOUGHT ME AND THE REBASE PAID ONE OF THEM. REDS.md stood at 40,947 against 40,960 when I went to book -- thirteen bytes, rows_that_fit=0. Rather than fold, I stashed and rebased onto xy, and a peer's fold in bc37657e8 took the pin to 35,694. The card had no such luck: my block went through six drafts from 1,300 bytes to 780 to fit 40,954 under 40,960, which is the same tax my last lap paid and reported.
