file construction/REDS.md the row booked -- it landed as %530 rather than %520, since this lap was parked at its round open and the spine spent four more numbers before a later lap recovered it; the stamp 20260906.225150 never moved, which is the derived-spine law working
file construction/ITINERARY.md the Petrichor block: the row, the loom, and the setting finding sized for your word -- the block that shipped is the recovering lap's, and it carries both questions forward
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- one question, and it is cheap to answer. `qa_report_card.sh` grades a page at whatever setting the runner types, and 305 living pages have already written down which setting they are. May the card read the page's own head when no flag is typed -- honouring a declared **Door** and **Field**, and refusing a declared **Meter**, since Meter sets both counted readings to 100 and a page declaring itself into that is granting itself the exemption rather than choosing a stricter budget? The instances are small (13 letters wrong, 3 crossing the B door) and the direction is the reason to ask: the default is the looser class, so the miss can only ever pass a page its own header says is failing.
scope closing the one real red the cold open found, building the loom for the class my own previous lap closed to a single spelling, and measuring -- rather than arguing -- the setting question the Earth row put in front of me
